# `${onlyConverted}`; plain = { held }; plain + 1; odd = { valueOf: somethingNoTableLists, given }; odd + 1
# Whatever an operation converts to a primitive lies in one hub, and the conversion calls what it finds on an object with that object as `this`. On one of the three a function nobody knows is found:
# that object is handed to it, so it escapes and what it holds is entered. Nothing of the kind is found on the other two: they stay in the program, and nobody enters the closure or what the plain object holds.
# converted-objects-past-those-told-apart-escape-together.ir has the same program with a limit that the hub passes.
# RUN: valueflow-solve unreached
# CHECK: unreached f1
# CHECK-NEXT: unreached f2
# CHECK-NOT: unreached f3
# RUN(ESCAPED): valueflow-why escaped=f1 escaped=f2 escaped=f3 escaped-layout=L0 escaped-layout=L1
# ESCAPED: escaped=f1
# ESCAPED-NEXT: not held
# ESCAPED: escaped=f2
# ESCAPED-NEXT: not held
# ESCAPED: escaped=f3
# ESCAPED-NEXT: n0 escaped
# ESCAPED: escaped-layout=L0
# ESCAPED-NEXT: escaped-layout=L1
# ESCAPED: n0 escaped
# PROGRAM-OF: converted-objects-past-those-told-apart-escape-together.ir
